      "3_4": "By the mid-1800s, the North and the South had grown apart. The North had many factories, while the South depended on plantations that used enslaved labor. Many people put their region above national unity, which is called sectionalism. In 1857, the Dred Scott decision ruled that Black people could not be citizens. After Abraham Lincoln was elected president in 1860, Southern states chose secession, the formal withdrawal of a state from the Union. The Civil War began in 1861. In 1863, the Emancipation Proclamation declared enslaved people in the rebel states free. Emancipation, the act of freeing enslaved people, became a goal of the war.",
